WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.132 --> 00:00:00.965
(audience cheering)

00:00:00.965 --> 00:00:02.070
- Have a seat.

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:04.264
- Hang on, I just want to visit
with Jane for a little bit.

00:00:04.264 --> 00:00:05.097
If that's okay.
- [Kelly] Okay fine.

00:00:05.097 --> 00:00:06.230
I get it, I get it.
- So I haven't you

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:07.335
since the last Hollywood

00:00:07.335 --> 00:00:08.168
- How is your family?
- Everybody,

00:00:08.168 --> 00:00:09.810
Hollywood Game Night.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.660
- I know all of us have been, I know.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:12.493
That's what you need.

00:00:12.493 --> 00:00:13.410
- The funnest game show ever.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:14.710
- [Jane] Oh good,
- [Kelly] I know.

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:15.820
- Ever.
- Well wait, we've all been

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:17.440
on Hollywood Game Night, a lot of us here,

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:18.700
but actually, a few of y'all have been

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:19.907
on Dancing with the Stars

00:00:19.907 --> 00:00:21.210
as well.
- Give it up.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.595
(audience cheers and drowns out talking)

00:00:23.595 --> 00:00:24.428
- I've given up dancing,
is that what you mean?

00:00:24.428 --> 00:00:27.270
- Yeah, that too.
- What was that like?

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:28.240
Like being on that show?
- I don't think

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.670
people understand how brutal that show is.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:32.550
- Oh no, it looks like

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:33.383
fat camp.
- [Jane] It was brutal,

00:00:33.383 --> 00:00:35.336
yeah, yeah.
- Yeah, to me.

00:00:35.336 --> 00:00:38.910
(audience hollers)

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:41.350
- You better get you some
of that sleeveless number.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:43.240
- God forbid they do
the picture of the dance

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:45.717
when I was in a tuxedo, no.

00:00:45.717 --> 00:00:47.267
- No, we want to embarrass you.

00:00:48.642 --> 00:00:49.570
- And they'll vouch for this,

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.620
is that the thing that was the weirdest

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:54.690
for me was if you got moved forward,

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:56.560
there was no, "I'll see
you in a couple days."

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:57.880
it was the next morning,

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:00.030
you were back in this dance hall.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:01.900
I figured out when I left that show,

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:03.930
when I got eliminated in the finals,

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.630
that I had danced six hours a day,

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:07.640
seven days a week for 13 weeks.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:08.560
- [Jane] Wow.
(audience whoops)

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.450
- [Kelly] Were you in incredible shape?

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:13.366
- No, no.
(audience laughs)

00:01:13.366 --> 00:01:14.930
- You were sore, your toes were sore.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:16.750
- And I was, I won't say my age,

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:18.750
but it was in the high 50s when I did it.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:21.701
Men my age, see they're young.

00:01:21.701 --> 00:01:25.180
Men my age aren't designed
to dance six hours a day,

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.430
seven days a week for 13 weeks.

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:28.980
We're designed to dance once a year,

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:30.276
drunk at a wedding.

00:01:30.276 --> 00:01:33.940
(audience laughs and claps)

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:35.917
- Jane, would you ever do dancing

00:01:35.917 --> 00:01:36.750
with the stars?
- I would not.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.420
If you hear that I'm doing
Dancing with the Stars,

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:40.980
you know there's something
really wrong with me.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:43.500
Absolutely not, I can't, I hate to dance.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.820
I hate people telling
me how to move my body

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:46.761
because I can't do it.

00:01:46.761 --> 00:01:47.594
- I feel like you would be so,

00:01:47.594 --> 00:01:48.540
not on the show, but like

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:49.373
so much fun.
- She would do it.

00:01:49.373 --> 00:01:51.427
- I'd be a big joke, that's what I'd be.

00:01:51.427 --> 00:01:52.260
- I want to go

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:53.093
dancing with you.
- [Bill] What do you

00:01:53.093 --> 00:01:53.926
think I was?

00:01:53.926 --> 00:01:55.250
- I'd be the Bill Engvall of it.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:58.770
- That was the best part of it

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:00.520
because I kept getting moved forward,

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.590
and what I always think is funny is,

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.110
if you go back and google the dances,

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:04.000
don't even watch the dance,

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.890
just go to when they call the scores out,

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:08.600
and look at the judges' face.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:09.650
Every time we got moved forward,

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:10.487
they had this look, like,

00:02:10.487 --> 00:02:12.065
"How is he still here?"

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.360
(audience laughs)

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.490
- But it's fan voted.
- It's fan voted.

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:18.630
And I had a blast.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:20.980
Emma, little Emma Slater was my partner,

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:23.441
and I would never, ever do it again.

00:02:23.441 --> 00:02:24.820
(audience laughs)

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:25.780
- [Jane] But God bless
you for doing it, though,

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:26.840
that is just amazing.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:29.830
- In 13 weeks, I tore my
groin, pulled my hamstring,

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:31.520
and had to have my knee replaced.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:34.593
- [Jane] Wow.
- And I say no sir to that.

00:02:34.593 --> 00:02:36.420
- [Bill] No ma'am.
- Nope, nope.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:37.920
So you're touring, though,

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:39.900
and your doing Last Man
Standing with Tim Allen.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.030
That show is hilarious.
- Great,

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:42.100
we have so much fun with it.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.632
- Yeah, are you having such a good time?

00:02:43.632 --> 00:02:44.580
Great cast?
- Yeah, play a character

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:45.790
called Reverend Paul that's kinda

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:47.230
become a reoccurring character,

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:49.850
and he's, Revered Paul's
probably the only guy

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.290
that can say things to Mike Baxter

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:55.800
that nobody else can say
because he's in the clergy.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.560
But it's been interesting.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.970
It's like kind of with
Dancing with the Stars,

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:01.017
I'm on the road now, people are like,

00:03:01.017 --> 00:03:02.370
"Hey, do another Last Man Standing."

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:04.058
It's amazing the popularity of the show,

00:03:04.058 --> 00:03:04.891
but it's a great show.

00:03:04.891 --> 00:03:06.010
- It's a great show.

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:07.864
- So hopefully they'll give me a lot more.

00:03:07.864 --> 00:03:08.697
(audience claps)

